    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286-a1-a7">

                <pb facs="0462" n="422" xml:id="pg422"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Wilding to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Liverpool,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 17, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> By direction of Mr. Dudley, I herewith
                    enclose copies of the opinions of counsel in the cases of the Tallahassee and
                    Sumter.</p>
                <p>Referring to my letter of yesterday, I sent you a telegram this morning informing
                    you that Thompson left here by the 9 o’clock train, this morning, for London;
                    intends shopping at Fischer’s hotel, Clifford street, and proceeding to France
                    to-morrow.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. WILDING, <hi rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., London,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
